From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:44:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: reuse abstract values and environments that do not
 change

Abstract1.change_environment copies the abstract value even when the
environment is unchanged, and the environment of an expression was rebuilt
for every evaluation although its variables are nearly always present
already. Return the value or the environment as it is in those cases, cache
the APRON variable of each analysed variable, and build array-cell names
without Format. Abstract values are never modified in place by the checker,
so sharing them is safe. Verdicts are unchanged.

Skipping the copy can change the order of the constraints APRON returns
for a relational value, and the safety report printed them in that order.
Print them sorted instead, so that the report depends on the value only.
The expected output of the safety tests changes in that order alone.

Signed-off-by: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
---
 compiler/safetylib/domains/safetyNum.ml | 67 +++++++++++++++----------
 compiler/safetylib/safetyVar.ml         | 26 +++++++---
 compiler/tests/safety/run.expected      | 36 ++++++-------
 3 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)

